@page "/demo/welcome"

<PageTitle>Welcome — Blazor Reference</PageTitle>

<div class="demo-page">

  <GupContentHeader PageTitle="Welcome to the Gov.om Blazor component library">
    <PageSummary>
      A Blazor-native implementation of the Gov.om (Government Unified Platform) design
      system, published as the <code>GUPBlazor</code> NuGet package.
    </PageSummary>
  </GupContentHeader>

  <div class="demo-body">

    <section class="demo-section">
      <p class="doc-lede">
        These pages document how to install and use the library. Pick a component from the
        sidebar to see it rendered, with the markup that produced it.
      </p>
      <p>
        The components are native Razor components — not wrappers around the upstream web
        components — so they work in Blazor Server, WebAssembly and Hybrid without any
        JavaScript interop beyond the small amount the library ships itself.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="demo-section">
      <h2 class="demo-section-title">What's included</h2>
      <ul class="doc-list">
        <li><strong>Razor components</strong> — @DemoNav.TotalCount reference pages covering the component set, each with live examples.</li>
        <li><strong>Design tokens</strong> — the full CSS custom property set for colour, typography and spacing. <a href="/demo/design-tokens">Browse the tokens</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Icons</strong> — Material Symbols Outlined, exposed through <code>GupIcon</code>. <a href="/demo/icons">See the icon set</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Accessibility</strong> — semantic markup, focus management and screen-reader affordances built into the components.</li>
        <li><strong>RTL and Arabic</strong> — every component is mirrored for right-to-left layouts.</li>
        <li><strong>Page templates</strong> — whole-page compositions for the shapes a service actually ships.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="demo-section">
      <h2 class="demo-section-title">Getting started</h2>
      <ul class="doc-list">
        <li><a href="/demo/installation">Installation</a> — add the package and wire up the styles and scripts.</li>
        <li><a href="/demo/usage">Usage</a> — utility components, spacing and icons.</li>
        <li><a href="/demo/design-tokens">Design tokens</a> — the variables behind every component.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="demo-section">
      <h2 class="demo-section-title">Browser support</h2>
      <p>
        All modern desktop and mobile browsers — Chrome, Firefox, Safari and Edge. The
        components rely on Blazor's own baseline, so anything that runs Blazor runs these.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="demo-section">
      <h2 class="demo-section-title">Hosting models</h2>
      <p>The same components work across every Blazor hosting model:</p>
      <ul class="doc-list">
        <li><strong>Blazor Server</strong> — interactive components over a SignalR circuit.</li>
        <li><strong>Blazor WebAssembly</strong> — the whole app in the browser.</li>
        <li><strong>Blazor Web App</strong> — per-component render modes, including static SSR.</li>
        <li><strong>Blazor Hybrid</strong> — MAUI, WPF and WinForms hosts.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="demo-section">
      <h2 class="demo-section-title">Relationship to the upstream design system</h2>
      <p>
        This library is a port of the
        <a href="https://github.com/Gov-om/design-system" target="_blank" rel="noopener">gov.om design system</a>,
        which ships web components for Angular, React and vanilla JavaScript. Component
        behaviour, markup and design tokens track upstream; the API is idiomatic Blazor
        rather than a one-to-one copy of the custom-element attributes.
      </p>
      <p>
        The upstream Storybook is the reference for visual and behavioural parity:
        <a href="https://storybook.service.gov.om/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">storybook.service.gov.om</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="demo-section">
      <h2 class="demo-section-title">Feedback</h2>
      <p>
        The library is under active development and welcomes feedback — see the
        <a href="/demo/feedback-contact">Feedback</a> page for how to reach the team.
      </p>
    </section>

  </div>
</div>
